---
# Firebase AI Logic server prompt template (dotprompt format).
# Template ID: template_plan_generate  → Remote Config key: template_plan_generate
# Called from src/ai/hybrid.ts runBigCloudJob() for plan-mode "generate a whole
# plan". The client sends templateVariables { request, preamble }; the CODE
# re-validates every returned room/door/window before it touches the scene, so
# this template only shapes the model, it is never trusted.
model: googleai/gemini-3.5-flash-lite
config:
  temperature: 0.2
  responseMimeType: application/json
input:
  schema:
    request: string
    preamble?: string
  default:
    preamble: ""
output:
  schema:
    unit?: string
    clarify?: string
    rooms(array):
      name: string
      x: number
      y: number
      w: number
      h: number
    doors?(array):
      room: string
      side: string
      width: number
    windows?(array):
      room: string
      side: string
      width: number
---
{{preamble}}
You design a whole, believable 2D home floor plan as ONE JSON DOCUMENT (NOT ops). Reply JSON only, no prose:
{"unit":"mm","rooms":[{"name":"Bedroom 1","x":0,"y":3000,"w":4000,"h":3000},{"name":"Bedroom 2","x":4000,"y":3000,"w":4000,"h":3000},{"name":"Living room","x":0,"y":0,"w":4000,"h":3000},{"name":"Kitchen","x":4000,"y":0,"w":2000,"h":3000},{"name":"Bathroom","x":6000,"y":0,"w":2000,"h":3000}],"doors":[{"room":"Living room","side":"s","width":900},{"room":"Bedroom 1","side":"s","width":800},{"room":"Bedroom 2","side":"s","width":800}],"windows":[{"room":"Bedroom 1","side":"n","width":1200},{"room":"Kitchen","side":"s","width":1000}]}
Rules: "rooms" is REQUIRED and non-empty. Each room is an axis-aligned rectangle; (x,y) is its bottom-left corner; w,h are width/height. TILE the rooms to fill one overall rectangle with NO OVERLAPS and NO GAPS — neighbours must share an EXACT edge (one room x=0 w=4000, its neighbour x=4000). Default "unit" is "mm" (a 4 m room is 4000). At most 8 rooms. A realistic flat has 2 bedrooms + a living room + a kitchen + a bathroom. Give it ONE entrance door (on an OUTER wall of the living room) and a door into each room; put windows only on OUTER walls (facing outside). "side" is n|s|e|w of that room's wall. CODE builds every wall, reuses shared walls, assigns all ids, dimensions and selects the wall shared by the two bedrooms — you ONLY place rooms, doors and windows. Never emit ops or ids, and never overlap two rooms. If the request is unclear, reply {"clarify":"<short question>"}.
Request: "{{request}}"
